 "intro": "Off Naulochus, on the north coast of Sicily, 3 September 36 BC. Sextus Pompeius, Pompey’s last son, rules the sea and starves Rome. You are Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa, Octavian’s admiral, with a new fleet trained in secret.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account, about 300 ships fought on each side while both armies watched from the shore. Agrippa’s heavier ships used the harpax, a grapnel fired from a catapult on an iron-bound line, to haul enemy ships close and board them. Sextus’s fleet was destroyed; only seventeen ships escaped. Sextus fled east and was killed. Lepidus then tried to seize Sicily, but his soldiers went over to Octavian, leaving Octavian and Antony to face each other. The other choices are what-ifs.",
